.TH gd_alter_chunk_size 3 "March 2026" "Version 0.12.0" "GETDATA"

.SH NAME
gd_alter_chunk_size \(em set the chunk size for a Dirfile fragment

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <getdata.h>
.HP
.BI "int gd_alter_chunk_size(DIRFILE *" dirfile ", off_t " chunk_size ,
.BI "int " fragment_index );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.FN gd_alter_chunk_size
function sets the chunk size (in frames) of the format specification fragment
given by
.ARG fragment_index
in the dirfile(5) database specified by
.ARG dirfile .
See the
.B /CHUNK
directive in
.BR dirfile\-format (5)
for details on chunked data storage.
.PP
The chunk size can only be set on fragments that are not already chunked
(i.e., whose current chunk size is zero).  Attempting to change the chunk size
of an already-chunked fragment will fail with
.BR GD_E_ARGUMENT .
To disable chunking, set
.ARG chunk_size
to zero.
.PP
In addition to being simply a valid fragment index,
.ARG fragment_index
may also be the special value
.BR GD_ALL_FRAGMENTS ,
which indicates that the chunk size of all fragments in the database should
be set.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Upon successful completion,
.FN gd_alter_chunk_size
returns zero.  On error, it returns a negative-valued error code.  Possible
error codes are:
.DD GD_E_ACCMODE
The specified dirfile was opened read-only.
.DD GD_E_ARGUMENT
The specified fragment is already chunked and a non-zero chunk size was given.
.DD GD_E_BAD_DIRFILE
The supplied dirfile was invalid.
.DD GD_E_BAD_INDEX
The supplied index was out of range.
.DD GD_E_RANGE
The supplied chunk size was negative.

.SH SEE ALSO
.F3 gd_open ,
.F3 gd_error ,
.F3 gd_error_string ,
dirfile(5),
dirfile-format(5)
